17:36:13 WARNING abductionbench.core.engine: dataset direct skipped: underlying notes require credentialed MIMIC-IV access -- The repository publishes 4 example annotated notes and the diagnostic knowledge graphs; the annotated MIMIC-IV discharge notes themselves need PhysioNet credentialed access, so a 300-item sample cannot be assembled from public data.
17:36:13 WARNING abductionbench.core.engine: dataset discoverybench skipped: gold hypotheses are withheld on every scorable split, and the task needs code execution -- Checked all four splits in the repository: real/test has 144 task files and synth/test 200, but their `hypotheses.main` entries are empty (0/144 and 0/200) -- the gold hypotheses are held back for the leaderboard. Only real/train carries hypotheses (14 files), which is both a train split and too small for a 300-item probe. Separately, a DiscoveryBench hypothesis is a quantitative claim ("positive with linear coefficient 0.82") that is derived by running statistical analyses over the shipped CSVs; a text-only single-turn harness cannot compute it, so scores would mostly measure guessing. Revisit if the authors publish test hypotheses and the engine gains a code-execution tool.
